1
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:03,200
Here, here.

2
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:05,880
This is Chenggong Pier.

3
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:06,680
Usually,

4
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,760
we locals

5
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,020
also like to come here and stroll around.

6
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,200
There's also a park behind here.

7
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,560
You guys can go down and walk around later

8
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:15,480
to experience

9
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,860
the slowness and openness of Nan'an.

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,640
By the way.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,360
That boat on the river,

12
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,600
everyone calls it

13
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,940
Chenggong Chuanshuo.

14
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:27,289
It's a moving scenery on the Xixi River in Nan'an.

15
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,280
Ms. Xing,

16
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,640
have you ever taken the Chenggong boat?

17
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:32,759
No.

18
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:34,280
What a coincidence.

19
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:36,200
You can try to take it today.

20
00:01:36,759 --> 00:01:37,320
No.

21
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:38,960
Let's go to the next spot.

22
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:39,479
Ms. Xing,

23
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:39,920
Feifei,

24
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,720
I think it's actually possible.

25
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,000
Xing Fei.

26
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:48,720
Have a seat.

27
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,479
Xing Fei.

28
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,780
Why do you always walk so fast?

29
00:01:57,039 --> 00:01:58,120
You're too slow.

30
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,760
But you told me before

31
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:07,530
that your favorite city is Nan'an.

32
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:09,860
Although it's very slow here,

33
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,380
it's a place where you can feel happy.

34
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:15,480
Xing Fei.

35
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,560
Walk slower.

36
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:21,740
At least during the time before we reach the end.

37
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:23,800
Okay.

38
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,380
Let's just part on good terms.

39
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,120
Look, there's more here.

40
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,880
Can you catch it?

41
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,490
You all think I'm very mean, don't you?

42
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:52,560
A little.

43
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,160
Just a little?

44
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,280
The relationship between people

45
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,640
is inherently about treating each other equally.

46
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,200
You work hard out there

47
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,160
and bear most of the household expenses.

48
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,280
He takes care of you

49
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,920
and provides emotional value.

50
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:08,840
It's very fair.

51
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,000
That's only fair to me.

52
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,730
What do you mean?

53
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,320
Wang Jun studied design.

54
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,890
He is very talented.

55
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,079
But to support my startup,

56
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,560
he quit his job at the design institute.

57
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,290
He revolves around me every day

58
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:27,340
and hasn't picked up a paintbrush in a long time.

59
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,700
He loves you very much.

60
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:33,020
Would you give up your dream for love?

61
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,320
Is this really love?

62
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,640
What must be faced, must be faced.

63
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:48,400
What must be faced, must be faced.

64
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,440
Mr. Wang.

65
00:03:58,880 --> 00:03:59,480
I'm fine.

66
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,320
She...

67
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,780
has always been like this.

68
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,450
No matter what happens,

69
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,850
she can always find the best solution.

70
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,880
She is very smart.

71
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:11,000
That's why I like her.

72
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:12,480
Then,

73
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,440
are you okay?

74
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,320
I'm fine. I'm fine.

75
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,980
After tomorrow's itinerary,

76
00:04:21,279 --> 00:04:22,880
we will officially break up.

77
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:26,090
I don't want to use her family card before the end.

78
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:27,700
It's too pathetic.

79
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,890
What does this have to do with the family card?

80
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,180
Director Li warned me privately,

81
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,480
telling me not to use your toilet paper.

82
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,460
She said your toilet paper

83
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,100
costs ten yuan a piece.

84
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,280
No,

85
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,760
I've washed my hands of that a long time ago.

86
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,760
What nonsense is she talking about?

87
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,400
To her,

88
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,480
I'm just a complete jerk.

89
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,800
What's wrong?

90
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,380
What's wrong with you?

91
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,200
I...

92
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,520
I'm fine.

93
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,400
Take it.

94
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,260
It's pretty cold outside.

95
00:05:39,159 --> 00:05:40,120
Thank you.

96
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,120
No need.

97
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,920
It's free.

98
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,040
I don't need it even if it's free.

99
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,520
What's wrong?

100
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,800
Nothing.

101
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,080
You and Zhang Yang...

102
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:30,360
Maybe we should just call it off.

103
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,960
Why so sudden?

104
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,360
It's not sudden.

105
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,760
I'm serious.

106
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,080
There are various reasons.

107
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,720
I'm not sure yet,

108
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,220
but it's pretty much decided.

109
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:46,960
No matter what,

110
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,280
I support you.

111
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,120
Tomorrow is the last day for the final order

112
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,250
before the new year.

113
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,240
Let's do our best.

114
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,520
The last day.

115
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,040
I heard you're still awake.

116
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:19,620
Is there a problem with your work?

117
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,280
I happen to be free today,

118
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:23,640
so I can do it with you.

119
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,200
No, thanks.

120
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,200
Thank you.

121
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,680
I'm sorry.

122
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,640
It was my fault before.

123
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:34,960
I wasn't good enough.

124
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,640
I don't blame you at all,

125
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,560
or mean to be angry with you.

126
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,680
I just think

127
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,680
that our way of getting along

128
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,730
should go back to the way it was before.

129
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,320
It's better when everyone is

130
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,860
more comfortable.

131
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,650
Please don't overthink it.

132
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,160
It has nothing to do with you.

133
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,060
It really doesn't.

134
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:12,720
Well,

135
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,880
it's not late.

136
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:18,500
It's getting late.

137
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,320
Go to bed early.

138
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,000
By the way,

139
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,240
this ring.

140
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,559
My sister saw it last time,

141
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,480
and I only knew about it after she mentioned it.

142
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,580
It's not cheap, right?

143
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,410
It's not appropriate for me to keep it.

144
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,520
You keep it.

145
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,740
It's better if you keep it.

146
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,840
You know, people are funny.

147
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,760
We're already divorced.

148
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:28,800
Yet on such a cold day,

149
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,530
I waited in line for three hours

150
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,450
just to buy this for you.

151
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,300
Do I have too much time on my hands?

152
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:38,720
Yes.

153
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:44,020
How are things with Qianqian?

154
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,040
Why bring her up?

155
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,980
We weren't a match.

156
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,610
We broke up ages ago.

157
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:52,900
Qian Cheng.

158
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,740
How come you were so shrewd when you were with me,

159
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,380
but with someone else,

160
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,000
before the wedding even happened,

161
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,060
you got scammed out of all your money?

162
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,040
What? Who told you that?

163
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,640
Bad news travels fast.

164
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,040
Don't listen to their nonsense.

165
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,760
Besides,

166
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,880
people shouldn't always look back.

167
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:15,010
We have to look forward.

168
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:16,440
In the past...

169
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:18,640
In the past,

170
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,080
besides me,

171
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,940
your favorite thing was this walnut cookie.

172
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,450
Do you remember?

173
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,330
When we first got together,

174
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:27,480
no matter how cold it was

175
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,880
or how long the line was,

176
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,740
I always made sure you got to eat this.

177
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,080
It was fun back then, too.

178
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,020
When I was with you,

179
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:40,730
I didn't even feel cold.

180
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,240
Yes.

181
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,280
In the past.

182
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,600
The tag is still on.

183
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:03,960
I have so many clothes at home.

184
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,600
Just grab one and it's brand new.

185
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,600
Stop pretending.

186
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,290
All your money was scammed,

187
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:10,280
and you're here reminiscing about the past with me.

188
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:10,920
Let me tell you.

189
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,640
The boss of this walnut cake shop has changed.

190
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,800
You don't need to queue anymore,

191
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:16,000
and it doesn't taste like this anymore.

192
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,040
Li Yiying,

193
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:18,040
stop right there.

194
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,810
Let me ask you one last time,

195
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,330
do you need a driver?

196
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,160
What about a security guard?

197
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:30,560
You.

198
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:35,050
A man kicked out is like spilled water.

199
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,760
Great,

200
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,570
now I can't return the clothes.

201
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,400
The beans in this cafe

202
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,940
are all locally selected,

203
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,360
and their pour-over technique is very particular.

204
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,890
We Nan'an people often say,

205
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,760
a cup of coffee brings half a day of leisure.

206
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:00,640
Staying here

207
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,720
makes you feel like time slows down.

208
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:06,400
So,

209
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:09,780
you need to leave some blank space in life

210
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,640
to savor more flavors.

211
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,520
You can understand it that way.

212
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:17,320
So,

213
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,920
whether it's coffee or something else,

214
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,000
it needs proper extraction and time,

215
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,010
as well as...

216
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,580
Once this cup is finished,

217
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,680
the next one won't be the same.

218
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,060
If you drink again,

219
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,760
it's a new cup.

220
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:48,840
Right?

221
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:56,880
Then,

222
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,900
congratulations.

223
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:01,720
Thank you.

224
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,400
Between us,

225
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,730
there's no need for thanks.

226
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:09,240
The words we've said

227
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,330
and the time we've spent

228
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:14,440
will be like the aroma of coffee,

229
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,250
staying in our memories

230
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:19,740
and influencing each other's future lives.

231
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,400
I understand.

232
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,280
I know.

233
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,840
It's just that you're walking too fast,

234
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,010
and I can't keep up anymore.

235
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:35,440
Wang Jun.

236
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,320
Let's each go and become

237
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,680
a complete,

238
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,400
new cup of coffee.

239
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,520
You will also find

240
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,210
someone who appreciates your flavor.

241
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:52,960
And I

242
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:57,360
must also adapt to the concentration I chose.

243
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,200
Zhang Yang.

244
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,720
If,

245
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,360
I mean if,

246
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,800
this cafe changed its coffee beans,

247
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,480
would you still come?

248
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,540
Even if the beans changed,

249
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,740
the cafe wouldn't change.

250
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,000
But,

251
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:38,600
changing the beans changes the taste.

252
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,760
Just because the beans changed,

253
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,480
does the cafe have no chance?

254
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,600
Maybe.

255
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:00,920
It's just the person drinking the coffee who changed.

256
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:11,840
Sis.

257
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,240
A few days ago,

258
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,320
I received an offer from

259
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:17,280
a large travel agency in Beijing.

260
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:20,370
The salary and benefits they offered are quite good.

261
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:21,880
I thought about it.

262
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:25,980
The career prospects are definitely better there.

263
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,180
Leaving things here in Nan'an to you,

264
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,460
I can rest assured.

265
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,600
Is that why you lost interest in him?

266
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,760
I didn't lose interest.

267
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:40,200
I just feel...

268
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,800
Long-distance relationships rarely work out.

269
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,400
Rather than getting heartbroken later,

270
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,240
I might as well not start it.

271
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:52,740
Good thing it hasn't started yet.

272
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,010
Does he know?

273
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,920
I haven't told him.

274
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,680
It's a bit

275
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,540
hard for me to bring up.

276
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:10,280
Xinyue.

277
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,290
Do you not believe in love anymore?

278
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:22,280
Everyone's fate is different.

279
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,700
I can't be your reference.

280
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:28,170
Just because I was wrong before

281
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,540
doesn't mean I'll be wrong in the future.

282
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,080
But right now, you are right.

283
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:34,570
You must cherish it.

284
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:38,840
But sister,

285
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,480
do you really think I'm right?
